ut_size[0],output_size[1], )(N, C, \text{output\_size}[0], \text{output\_size}[1], \dots)(N,C,output_size[0],output_size[1],) or (C,output_size[0],output_size[1], )(C, \text{output\_size}[0], \text{output\_size}[1], \dots)(C,output_size[0],output_size[1],) as described above Examples: >>> fold = nn.Fold(output_size=(4, 5), kernel_size=(2, 2)) >>> input = torch.randn(1, 3 * 2 * 2, 12) >>> output = fold(input) >>> output.size() torch.Size([1, 3, 4, 5]) extra_repr()[source]# Return the extra representation of the module. Return type str forward(input)[source]# Runs the forward pass. Return type Tensor
